      "writtenOn": "2026-10-03T06:07:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Staged: https://review.lineageos.org/c/LineageOS/android_device_motorola_beckham/+/506063 . It only touches beckham\u0027s tree; the blobs come from beckham_retail like the rest (they were in TheMuppets lineage-20), so the vendor repo needs regenerating for the test build.\n\nAbout 422116: it\u0027s in my build and fixes the dock volume. My issue is device selection: AudioService\u0027s readDockAudioSettings() (boot, user switch) and onAudioServerDied() set FOR_DOCK to FORCE_DIGITAL_DOCK when DOCK_AUDIO_MEDIA_ENABLED\u003d1, and the legacy policy only picks ANLG_DOCK_HEADSET for media with FORCE_ANALOG_DOCK. So even with the stock HAL, media goes to the speaker unless something sets ANALOG_DOCK (my app does). A framework tweak in the same spirit as 422116 (e.g. a config to use FORCE_ANALOG_DOCK there) could replace the app. Happy to write it if that sounds acceptable.",
      "parentUuid": "74a56395_882fee48",
      "revId": "6f43c21cc0ceb2ecd2b3dc5169656d00dc979b54",
